{"id": "section-body-27122", "title": "Panic Disorder", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-three", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MENTAL HEALTH CONDITIONS", "Psychiatric Disorders in Pregnancy", "Panic Disorder"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-27122", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Panic Disorder", "runs": [{"text": "Panic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disorder"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27123", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Some women may experience first-onset panic disorder during pregnancy. Women presenting with panic attacks for the first time should be screened for thyroid disorder. The correlation between plasma levels of cortisol in the mother and in the fetus may have implications for the developing fetal brain.", "runs": [{"text": "Some women may experience first-onset panic disorder during pregnancy. Women presenting with panic attacks for the first time should be screened for thyroid disorder. The correlation between plasma levels of cortisol in the mother and in the fetus may have implications for the developing fetal brain."}]}, {"id": "body-27125", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27126", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cognitive behavioral therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Cognitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behavioral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27127", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Supportive psychotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Supportive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27128", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Relaxation techniques", "runs": [{"text": "Relaxation"}, {"te